# Where the PUBG: BATTLEGROUNDS catalog comes from

Everything here was read on **2026-10-24** (D474). `catalog.json` is the single-kind
form (`kind: "weapons"`). The game is **PUBG: BATTLEGROUNDS** on PC and console
(PlayStation 4/5, Xbox One/Series), NOT PUBG Mobile (another game).

## The list: pubg.com's Arsenal page

KRAFTON's own [Arsenal page](https://pubg.com/en/game-info/weapons) lists every
current weapon with its ammo, a render and a per-weapon "last update" date (the
newest, 08-12-2026, is the RPD). The catalog is that list (58 items: 13 assault
rifles, 7 DMRs, 8 SMGs, 5 sniper rifles, 6 shotguns, 5 handguns, 3 LMGs, the
launchers, Crossbow, Stun Gun, Flare Gun and 5 melee weapons). Throwables
(grenades, smokes, Molotov, ...) are not in it: the Core's reader reads the gun
slots (D474), and a throwable in hand reads as nothing.

- **Latest update:** [43.2](https://pubg.com/en/news/11136), live on PC
  2026-10-14 and on console 2026-10-22. No weapon change.
- **Newest gun:** the **RPD** (LMG, 7.62 mm, full auto), [42.3](https://pubg.com/en/news/10885),
  PC 2026-08-12, console 2026-08-20; the 2026 roadmap's "August weapon".
- **Removed** in [42.1](https://pubg.com/en/news/10179) (announced in
  [41.1](https://pubg.com/en/news/9926) and [41.2](https://pubg.com/en/news/10080)),
  so NOT in the catalog:

