## Pictures: KRAFTON's own renders (D116, D474)

Every picture in `weapons/` is the render pubg.com's Arsenal page shows for the
weapon, from KRAFTON's host `wstatic-prod.pubg.com` (WebP, 1600 x 1096 RGBA),
cropped to the weapon (transparent border off, 4 px kept) and scaled to fit
480 x 300 as PNG, transparency kept. None is generated or from a fan site.
They are KRAFTON's copyright, used in the app to identify the weapon; the owner
decided on 2026-10-24 to use the real official art and handle licensing later
(D474). The Flare Gun has no Arsenal render: its picture is KRAFTON's own item art from
PUBG's official developer repository [github.com/pubg/api-assets](https://github.com/pubg/api-assets)
(`Assets/Item/Weapon/Handgun/Item_Weapon_FlareGun_C.png`, served by GitHub's
raw host), the same art the PUBG API's telemetry names.

The Core never receives any of these (pictures stay in the app). Its reader
learns from real gameplay frames only (D474, ZeroStick Model Library\PUBG).

